+/* Re:Fine patches/0143: the output follows the Windows default device (or a fixed one,
+ * REFINE_AUDIO_DEVICE). The mixing thread never opens, closes or waits on a device:
+ * the "audio device" thread prepares the new stream and hands it over, and the
+ * mixing thread picks it up between two blocks and hands the old one back. Its
+ * 5.33 ms schedule and the 0130 wait do not notice.
+ *
+ * The new stream starts with the last AUDIO_QUEUE_TARGET frames of the mix instead
+ * of silence: they are what the old device still had queued, so the sound goes on
+ * from there, and if the old device died, those frames were never heard. */
